<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.0">
  <book code="RUT" style="id">Ruth</book>
  <para style="h">Ruth</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ruth</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ruth</para>
  <para style="mt">Ruth</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Rorêltute chuan ro an rêl laiin heti hi a ni a, chumi ramah chuan ṭâm a lo tla a. Tin, Bethlehem-juda-a mi pakhat Moab rama awm tûrin amah leh a nupui leh a fapate pahnih nên an kal a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Chu mi hming chu Elimeleka a ni a, a nupui hming chu Naomi a ni a, a fapate pahniha hming chu Mahlona leh Kiliona, Bethlehem-juda-a Ephrath mi an ni. Moab ramah chuan an kal a, chutah chuan an awm ta reng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Tin, Elimeleka, Naomi pasal chu a thi a, amah leh a fapate pahnih chauh an ni ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Tin, Moab ram hmeichhia nupuiah an nei a: a pakhata hming chu Orpi a ni a, a pakhata hming chu Ruthi a ni; chutah chuan kum sâwm emaw lai an awm a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Tin, Mahlona leh Kiliona chu an thi ta ve ve a; tichuan, chu hmeichhia chu a fate pahnih leh a pasal chuan an thihsan ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Chutichuan, a mote nên chuan Moab ram ata chu haw leh tûrin an tho va, Lalpan ei tûr pein a mite chu a kan dân te Moab ram aṭanga a lo hriat avângin.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Tichuan, a awmna ata chu a mote pahnih nên chuan an chhuak a; Judai rama haw leh tûrin an kal ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan a mote pahnih hnênah chuan, “In nu in lam ve vea haw leh tûrin kal rawh u khai; mitthi chung leh ka chunga in tih ang hian Lalpa chuan in chungah ngilnei takin ti ve rawh se.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Lalpa chuan in pahnihin pasalte ina khawsakna in tawn theih nân khawngaih che u rawh se,” a ti a. Tichuan, a fâwp a; tin, aw chhuah meuhvin an ṭap ta chiam mai a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Tin, a hnênah, “Kan kal lo vang, i chite hnêna i hâwnnaah chuan kan tel ve zâwk ang,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan, “Ka fanute u, haw leh zâwk rawh u; engah nge ka hnênah chuan in kal ve tehlul ang le? In pasal tûr fapa ka pai leh thei dâwn em ni?
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Ka fanute u, haw leh ula, kal rawh u khai; pasal han nei tûrin ka upa lutuk tawh si a. Tin, ka bei a la sei reng e ti mah ila, zâninah mai pawh hian pasal neiin fapate pawh nei mah ila,
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />an puitlin thlengin in awm dâwn em ni ang? Pasal lovin in awm reng dâwn em ni ang? Ni kawng lo ve a, ka fanute u, nangmahni avâng hian ka lungngaihna a zualkai zâwk a ni, Lalpa kut chu ka chungah a tla ta a nih hi,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Tin, an aw chhuahin an ṭap leh ta chiam mai a; tin, Orpi chuan a pi chu a fâwp a, Ruthi erawh chuan a vuan tlat a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, “Ngai teh, i mopuinu chu a chite hnên leh a pathian hnên lamah chuan a kîr leh ta a; nang pawh i mopuinu ûmin haw ve tawh aw,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tin, Ruthi chuan, “Nangmah ṭhen tûr leh nangmah zui lova haw leh tûr chuan mi thlêm lo hrâm hrâm rawh; i kalna apiangah ka kal ang a; i riahna apiangah ka riak ang a; i chite chu ka chite an ni ang a, i Pathian chu ka Pathian a ni ang.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />I thihna apiangah chuan ka thi ang a, chutah chuan mi phûm ve mai tûr a ni. Nang leh kei hi thihna chauh lo chuan thil dangina min ṭhen dâwn chuan Lalpan a tih tihin mi ti mai sela, chu aia nasa pawhin,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Chutichuan, a hnêna kal a tum tlat tih a lo hriat chuan a ngawihsan ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Tichuan, Bethlehem thlengin an kal dûn ta a. Tin, heti hi a ni a, Bethlehem an thlen chuan a khuain an phu ta mur mur mai a, hmeichhiate chuan, “Hei, Naomi kha a ni maw?” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Ani chuan an hnênah, “Naomi min ti suh u, Marai min ti zâwk rawh u. Engkimtitheia chuan lungchhiatthlâk takin min ti ta si a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Muk takin ka chhuak a, Lalpa chuan kutbêngin mi hruai hâwng leh a ni. Lalpa chuan ka chungah a lungnih lohna a tilang a, Engkimtitheia chuan mi tihhrehawm te hre reng siin, engati nge Naomi min la tih cheu ni le?” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Chutichuan, Naomi chu a lo kîr a, a monu Moab mi Ruthi nên Moab ram aṭang chuan an lo kîr a ni. Barli seng ṭan tirh laiin Bethlehem chu an thleng a ni.
  </para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan a pasala laichîn, Elimeleka thlah, mi neinung tak laichîn a nei a; a hming chu Boaza a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Tin, Moab mi Ruthi chuan Naomi hnênah, “Lo lamah ka kal ang a, mi lo khawngaihtu apiang buhṭo ka va zawng ang e aw?” a ti a. Tin, a hnênah, “Kal ta che, ka fanu,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Tichuan, a kal ta a, buh sengtute seng hmaih chu a va zawng ta a. Elimeleka thlah Boaza lovah ngei chuan a va kal fu hlauh mai a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Tichuan, ngai teh, Bethlehem aṭangin Boaza chu a va kal a, buh sengtute hnênah chuan, “In hnênah Lalpa awm rawh se,” a ti a. Tin, anni chuan, “ Lalpan malsâwm che rawh se,” tiin an chhâng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Chutichuan, Boaza chuan a chhiahhlawh, buh sengtute chunga hotu hnênah chuan. “Hei khawi lam nula nge ni le?” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Tin, a buh sengtute chunga hotu a chhiahhlawh chuan, “Moab nula, Moab ram ata Naomi hnêna lo kal ve a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, ‘Min khawngaih la, in buhṭo ka zawng ang a, buh sengtuten an buhphal an khâwm zawhin ka zawng zêl ang e,’ a ti a; tichuan, a lo kal a, ina rei lo tê a han awm tih loh chu zîng ata a la awm ta reng a ni,” tiin a chhâng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Chutichuan, Boaza chuan Ruthi hnênah chuan, “Ka fanu, ngai teh aw, lo dangah chuan buhṭo zawngin kal suh la, heta ta hi kal sawn suh, ka chhiahhlawh nulate hnênah hian awm reng rawh.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />An buh seng hi en reng la, an hnu chhui zêl rawh; tlangvâlte chu eng mah tih loh tûr chein thu ka pe tawh diam e; tin, i tui a hâl apiangin tuibêla tlangvalte tui chawi sa va in ṭhîn ang che,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Chutichuan, a kûn a, lei siin a bawkkhup a, a hnênah, “Hnam dang ka ni si a, nangin hetianga min hriat duha min lo khawngaih hi eng tizia nge ni?” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Tin, Boaza chuan a chhâng a, a hnênah, “I pasal thih achin i pi chunga i thiltih dân zawng zawngte miin mi hrilh vek a; tin, i nu leh i pa leh i pianna ram kalsana tûn hma lama i mi hriat ngai lohte hnêna i lo kal dânte pawh hi.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Lalpa chuan i thiltih chu rûl sela, Lalpa , Israel-te Pathian, inhumhim nâna a thla hnuai i rawn chuha chuan i ṭhat man pe ṭeuh che rawh se,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, “Ka pu, mi khawngaih ang che; nangin mi thlamuan a, i chhiahhlawh nulate zînga mi ni mah suh ila, i chhiahhlawhnu hi ṭha takin mi be ta si a,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Tin, chaw ei hun chuan Boazan a hnênah, “Lo haw teh khai, chhangte hi han ei ve la, chhang themte chu uain thûrah han chiah ve rawh,” a ti a. Chutichuan, buh sengtute kiangah chuan a ṭhu a; tin, chhangpêr chu an pe a, a ei a, a kham hnu pawhin a la ei bâng ta cheu va.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Tin, buhṭo zawng tûra a thawh leh chuan, Boaza chuan a tlangvâlte hnênah, “Buhphal zînga mite pawh hi chhar zêl sela, hau suh ang che u.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tin, a têla mite pawh, pawh chhuahsak ula, hnutchhiah zêl ula, chhar sela, hau suh u,” tiin thu a pe a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Chutichuan, lova buhṭo chu tlai lam thlengin a zawng a; tin, a zawn sa chu a vua a, barli epha khat emaw lai a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Tin, a phur a, khuaah chuan a haw ta a, a pi chuan a buhṭo zawn chu a lo hmu a. Tin, ani chuan a kham hnua a ei bâng chu a phawrh a, a pe a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Tin, a pi chuan a hnênah, “Vawiinah hian khawi lama buhṭo nge i zawn? A lo hre duhtu che chu malsâwmin awm rawh se,” a ti a. Tin, ani chuan, tu hnênah nge a va thawh tih a pi chu a hrilh a, “Vawiina ka va thawhna pa chu a hming Boaza a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan a monu hnênah chuan, “ Lalpa , mi nung leh mitthi chunga a khawngaihna bâng chuang ngai lova chuan amah chu malsâwm rawh se,” a ti a. Tin, Naomi chuan a hnênah, “Chu mi chu kan lamhnai, kan laichîn bul a ni asin,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Tin, Moab mi Ruthi chuan, “A nih tak chu, ka hnênah pawh, ‘Ka buh hi an seng zawh vek hma loh chu ka tlangvâlho hnênah hian tel reng ang che,’ mi ti nghe nghe asin,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan a monu Ruthi hnênah chuan, “Ka fanu, lo danga an hmuh hauh lohna tûr chein a chhiahhlawh nulaho zîngah hlîr chuan kal la a ṭha ang,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Chutichuan, barli leh huit seng zawh thlengin Boaza chhiahhlawh nulaho zîngah hlîr chuan buhṭo zawngin a kal a; tin, a pi hnênah chuan a awm a.
  </para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Tin, a pi Naomi chuan a hnênah, “Ka fanu, i tâna ṭha tûr khawsakna ka zawnsak dâwn lâwm che ni?
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Kan laichînpa Boaza, a chhiahhlawh nulate nêna hna i va thawhna kha a awm a ni lâwm ni? Ngai teh, zâninah hian hruihah barli a zâp fai dâwn a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Chutichuan, inbual la, inthih la, i incheina puan sin la, hruihah chuan zuk kal rawh; amaherawhchu, chaw te a eia a in zawh hma loh chuan a hnênah inhriattîr hauh suh ang che.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Tin, heti hi a ni ang a, a mut hunah chuan a mutna chu chhinchhiah la; tin, lût la, a ke hlîm la, mu rawh; tin, ani chuan i tih tûr chu a lo hrilh ang che,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan a hnênah, “I sawi apiang chu ka ti ang e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Tichuan, hruihah chuan a zuk kal a, a piin a hrilh ang apiang chuan a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Tin, Boaza chuan chaw a ei a, a in zawh chuan a rilru a lo hlim ta êm êm a, buh vûm bulah chuan mu tûrin a kal ta a; tin, zawi têin a va kal a, a ke chu a hlîm a, a mu ve ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Tin, heti hi a ni a, zanlaiah chuan chu pa chuan a hlau va, lehlam a hawi a; tin, ngai teh, a ke bulah chuan hmeichhia a lo mu reng mai a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, “Tu nge i nih?” a ti a. Ani chuan, “I chhiahhlawhnu Ruthi ka ni; chutichuan, i chhiahhlawhnu hi i puan mi han zâwn rawh, ka laichîn bul i ni si a,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, “Ka fanu, Lalpan malsâwm che rawh se! Tlangvâl rethei emaw, hausa emaw i zui loh dânah hian a tîr ai mahin a hnu lamah hian ṭhatna i tilang nasa ta zâwk a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Chutichuan, ka fanu, hlau suh aw. I sawi ang zêlin i chungah ka ti ang, kan khuaa mi zawng zawngte hian hmeichhe fel tak i ni tih an hre vek si a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Tin, laichîn inhnai kan ni ngei mai a; amaherawhchu, keimah aia hnai zâwk a awm a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Zânin chu awm phawt la, naktûk zîngah chuan i chungah ani chuan a laichîn tih tûr a tih duh chuan a ṭha a ni ang a; laichîn pual chu ti ang hmiang. Amaherawhchu, laichîn tih tûr chu i chunga a tih duh loh chuan, laichîn tih tûr chu Lalpa a nung ngei ang hian keiman ka ti ngei ang! Zîng thlengin mu reng mai rawh,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Tichuan, zîng thlengin a ke bulah chuan a mu ta a; tin, tu mah la inhmuh chian theih hmain a tho va, “Hruihah chuan hmeichhia chu a lo kal tih rêng rêng tu mân hre suh se,” a ti rêng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Tin, a hnênah, “I puan bah kha han la la, dawh rawh,” a ti a. Tichuan, a dawh a, barli chu tehkhâwng rûkin a teh a, a chhûng a; tin, khuaah a kal ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tin, a pi hnên a han thlen chuan, “Ka fanu, eng nge i an le?” a lo ti a. Tin, ani chuan chu pain a chunga thil a lo tih zawng zawng chu a hrilh a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />“He barli tehkhâwng ruk hi min pe a, ‘I pi hnênah chuan kutbêngin haw hauh suh ang che,’ min ti a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Tin, ani chuan, “Ka fanu, eng angin nge thil a lo awm dâwn i hriat hma loh chuan awm mai rawh; vawiina he thil hi a tih zawh hma loh chuan chu pa chu a ngawi mai dâwn si lo va,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Tichuan, Boaza chu kulh kawngkaah chuan a han chho va, chutah chuan a ṭhu a; tin, ngai teh, an laichîn bul a chungchâng thu Boazan a sawi kha a lo kal a. Chu mi hnênah chuan, “E! Nang kha, lo pêng la, ṭhu teh khai,” a ti a. Tin, ani chu a lo pêng a, a ṭhu ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Tin, chumi khuaa upaho zînga mi sâwm a hruai a, an hnênah, “Hetah hian ṭhu teh u khai,” a ti a, an ṭhu ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Tin, an laichîn bula hnênah chuan, “Moab ram aṭanga lo kîr Naomi chuan kan unaupa Elimeleka ram kha a zuar a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />tichuan, i hnêna, ‘Hênga ṭhute mit hmuhah leh kan upateho mit hmuhah hian lei rawh. I tlan duh chuan tlan la; amaherawhchu, i tlan duh loh chuan ka hriat theih nân min hrilh ang che; nang lo chu tu mah a han tlantu âwm dang an awm si lo va; tin, kei hi i dawtah chuan ka ni a,’ tia hriattîr che ṭûlin ka hria,” a ti a. Tin, ani chuan, “Ka tlan ang e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Tin, Boaza chuan, “Naomi hnêna mi, chumi ram i lei ni chuan mitthi nupui, Moab hmeichhia Ruthi lakah mitthi hming dai lova a ro luahtu tûr an awm zêl theih nân i lei bawk tûr a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />An laichîn bul pa chuan, “Keima tân chuan ka tlan thei lo; chuti lo zawng, keima roluah lam thu ka tikhawlo dah ang e, tlan phâk ka nihna ai chu nangman chang mai rawh; kei zawngin ka tlan thei lo a nih hi,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Hmânlaia Israel-te zîngah thil engkim an tihngheh nâna an intlan dân leh an inthleng dân chu hetiang hi a ni: pheikhawk an hlîp a, an vêngte an pe a, chu chu Israel-te zînga an tihngheh dân a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Chutichuan, an laichîn bul chuan Boaza hnênah, “Nangman i tân lei zâwk rawh,” a ti a. Tin, a pheikhawk a hlîp a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Tin, Boaza chuan upate leh mipui zawng zawngte hnênah chuan, “Vawiinah hian nangniho hi Elimeleka thil neih zawng zawng leh Kiliona leh Mahlona thil neih zawng zawng, Naomi hnêna mi ka lei tih hretute in ni a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Tin, chu chauh chu ni lovin, mitthi chu a hming dai lova ro luahtu siamsak tûr leh, mitthi chu a unaute zîngah leh a awmna hmun kulh kawngkaa a hming a bo loh nân Moab hmeichhia Ruthi, Mahlona nupui chu ka nupui atân ka lei a; chu chu vawiinah hian nangniho hi a hretute in ni e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Tin, kulh kawngkaa mipui zawng zawng leh upate chuan, “Hretute kan ni e. I ina hmeichhe lo lûta chu Rakili leh Leaii, Israel chhûngkaw dintu pahnihte ang khân Lalpa chuan siam rawh se; tin, Ephratha-ah chuan chhuanawm takin ti la, Bethlehem-ah chuan hmingthang takin lo awm ang che.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Tin, Lalpan he nula laka thlah a la siamsak tûr che avâng hian, i chhûngkua chu Tamarin Juda a hrinsak Pereza chhûngkua ang lo ni rawh se,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Chutichuan, Boaza chuan Ruthi chu a hruai a, a nupui a lo ni ta a; tin, a pâwl a, Lalpa chuan nau a paitîr a; tin, fapa a hring a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Tin, hmeichhiate chuan Naomi hnênah chuan, “Vawiin ngeia laichîn hnai chham lova awmtîrtu che Lalpa chu fakin awm sela; Israel-te zîngah hian a hming lo thang rawh se.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Tin, ani chu i nunna tungdingtu leh i tar lam châwmtu a lo ni ang a; i monu, nangmah hmangaihtu, fapa pasarih aia i tâna ṭha chuan amah chu a hring ta si a,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tin, Naomi chuan nau chu a la a, a pawm a, a awm ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Tin, a vêngte hmeichhia chuan a hming an saksak a, “Naomi tân fapa a lo piang,” tiin a hmingah Obeda an sa a. Ani chu Davida pa Jesaia pa a ni a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Hêng hi Pereza thlahte chu an ni: Pereza chuan Hezrona a hring a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Hezrona chuan Rama a hring a, Rama chuan Aminadaba a hring a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Aminadaba chuan Nasona a hring a, Nasona chuan Salmona a hring a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Salmona chuan Boaza a hring a; Boaza chuan Obeda a hring a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Obeda chuan Jesaia a hring a; tin, Jesaia chuan Davida a hring a ni.
  </para>
</usx>
